\begin_layout Proof
Let 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 be a binary relation on a set 
\begin_inset Formula $X$
\end_inset

.
 Assume 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 is complete and transitive.
 We want to prove that 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ \emptyset\neq B\subseteq X:C^{\succsim}(B)=C^{\succ}(B)$
\end_inset

.
 Take 
\begin_inset Formula $B\subseteq X$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula $B\neq\emptyset$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof

\series bold
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $(\subseteq)$
\end_inset

 
\series default
Take 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in C^{\succsim}(B)$
\end_inset

.
 Then, 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ y\in B:x\succsim y$
\end_inset

.
 We wish to show that 
\begin_inset Formula $\nexists\ y\in B:y\succ x$
\end_inset

.
 Suppose for contradiction 
\begin_inset Formula $\exists\ y\in B:y\succ x$
\end_inset

.
 Then, 
\begin_inset Formula $\exists\ y\in B:(y\succsim x)\ \wedge\ \neg(x\succsim y)$
\end_inset

.
 However, this contradicts 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ y\in B:x\succsim y\ (\rightarrow\leftarrow)$
\end_inset

 .
 So, 
\begin_inset Formula $\nexists\ y\in B:y\succ x$
\end_inset

.
 Thus, 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in C^{\succ}(B)$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof

\series bold
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $(\supseteq)$
\end_inset

 
\series default
Take 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in C^{\succ}(B)$
\end_inset

.
 Then, 
\begin_inset Formula $\nexists\ y\in B:y\succ x$
\end_inset

.
 From the definition of 
\begin_inset Formula $\succ$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\nexists\ y\in B:(y\succsim x)\ \wedge\ \neg(x\succsim y)$
\end_inset

.
 Equivalently, 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ y\in B:\neg(y\succsim x)\ \vee\ (x\succsim y)$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
